lesson: 102
title: Several equal parts of a set
stars: 0
explain: Two thirds means two of the three equal parts. First find one part, then take as many parts as the fraction says.
explain: Three fourths of 20 stickers: one fourth is 20 ÷ 4 = 5, so three fourths is 3 × 5 = 15.
vars: a=name t=thing p=3..6 m=2..5 n=6..60
need: m < p
need: (p != 6 || m == 5) && (p != 4 || m != 2)
need: n % p == 0
answer: n / p * m
exercise: What is {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of {n} {t}?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}, and {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of them are green. How many {t} are green?
exercise: {a} gives away {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of {a.his} {n} {t}. How many {t} does {a.he} give away?
exercise: There are {n} {t} in a jar. {a} takes {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of them. How many {t} does {a.he} take?
exercise: {a} shares {n} {t} into {p} equal piles and keeps {m} of the piles. How many {t} does {a.he} keep?
exercise: In a big box there are {n} {t}, and {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of them are new. How many new {t} are there?
test: A shelf holds {n} {t}; {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of them belong to {a}. How many of the {t} belong to {a.him}?
test: How many {t} are {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of a set of {n} {t}?
test: {a} counted {n} {t} and found that {m.words} {p.ordwords}s were broken. How many {t} were broken?
test: Out of {n} {t}, {a} picks {m.words} {p.ordwords}s. How many {t} are picked?
exercise: How many {t} are {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of {n} {t}?
